{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {x}^{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={x}^{2}-1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n${x}^{2}=u+1.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (u+1)\\cdot \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (u+1){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{3/2}+{u}^{1/2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}+\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-3568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-12497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int x\\sqrt{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-12497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=3x+1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=\\frac{u-1}{3}.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{u-1}{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int ({u}^{3/2}-{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{1}{5/2}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{1}{3/2}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{45}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{27}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{45}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{27}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-12497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-12497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-12497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+С"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{45}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{27}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{45}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+С"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{27}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-12497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{45}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{27}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-113751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $u=x+1,$ which integral is equivalent to $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-113751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u=x+1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe also note that \n$x=u-1.$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{(u-1)^{2}}{\\sqrt{u}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{2}-2u+1){u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{3/2}-2{u}^{1/2}+{u}^{-1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{u}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-113751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-113751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-113751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}-2\\sqrt{u})\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{u})\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{u}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{u})\\,\\text{d}u"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-113751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{u}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-2621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral of $(2x+1)\\sqrt{4-x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-2621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=4-x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=4-u.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+1)\\sqrt{4-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2(4-u)+1)\\sqrt{u}(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int (9-2u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int (9{u}^{1/2}-2{u}^{3/2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-(6{u}^{3/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{u}^{5/2})+C \\\\  & =-6\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{5}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-2621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-2621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-2621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{5}}+C"] ["math" "-8\\sqrt{(2x+1)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(2x+1)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "-\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{5}}+C"] ["math" "3\\sqrt[3]{4-x}-\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{(2x+1)^{3}}-\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(2x+1)^{5}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-2621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{5}}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the integral of $x\\sqrt{x-2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=x-2.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=u+2.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (u+2)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3/2}+2{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}+\\frac{4}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-3566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{x-2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-3566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-348275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}\\frac{7}{4}x\\sqrt[3]{6x+6}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-348275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=6x+6.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=\\frac{1}{6}(u-6).$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $-1$ | $1/3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $0$ | $8$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}\\frac{7}{4}x\\sqrt[3]{6x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}(u-6)\\cdot {u}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{144}{\\int }_{0}^{8}({u}^{4/3}-6{u}^{1/3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{144}{(\\frac{1}{(7/3)}{u}^{7/3}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{(4/3)}{u}^{4/3})|}_{0}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{144}{(\\frac{3}{7}{u}^{7/3}-\\frac{9}{2}{u}^{4/3})|}_{0}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{144}[(\\frac{3}{7}\\cdot {8}^{7/3}-\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot {8}^{4/3})-(\\frac{3}{7}\\cdot {0}^{7/3}-\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot {0}^{4/3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{144}(\\frac{384}{7}-72) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{144}\\cdot (-\\frac{120}{7}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-348275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-348275" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-348275" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{5}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-49529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $u=2x-1$, which integral is equivalent to ${\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\sqrt{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-49529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u=2x-1$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=\\frac{u+1}{2}.$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $1$ | $5$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\sqrt{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{u+1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{5}(u+1){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{5}({u}^{3/2}+{u}^{1/2})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-49529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-49529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-49529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}({u}^{3/2}+{u}^{1/2})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{5}({u}^{1/2}+{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{5}({u}^{3/2}+{u}^{1/2})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-49529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{5}({u}^{3/2}+{u}^{1/2})\\text{d}u"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-13191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{(x+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-13191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=x+2.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=u-2.$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $-2$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{(x+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(u-2){u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({u}^{4}-2{u}^{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{5}{u}^{5}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{u}^{4})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{5}{u}^{5}-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{4})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({2}^{5}-{0}^{5})-\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{4}-{0}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(32-0)-\\frac{1}{2}(16-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}-8 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-13191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-13191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-13191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{32}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{8}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{72}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-13191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{8}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-17045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\sqrt{{(2-x)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-17045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=2-x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=2-u.$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\sqrt{{(2-x)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x{(2-x)}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{0}(2-u){u}^{3/2}(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{0}(u-2){u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{0}({u}^{5/2}-2{u}^{3/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{7}{u}^{7/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2})|}_{2}^{0} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{7}{u}^{7/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{u}^{5/2})|}_{2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}({0}^{7/2}-{2}^{7/2})-\\frac{4}{5}({0}^{5/2}-{2}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{2}^{9/2}}{7}+\\frac{{2}^{9/2}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{11/2}}{35} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{11}}}{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-17045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-17045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-17045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{7}}}{35}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{9}}}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{11}}}{35}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{11}}}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{9}}}{35}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-17045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{11}}}{35}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-348282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{48(x+2)}{{({x}^{2}+4x)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-348282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={x}^{2}+4x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x+4\\,⟹\\,2(x+2)\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $-3$ | $-2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{48(x+2)}{{({x}^{2}+4x)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =24{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{1}{{({x}^{2}+4x)}^{3}}\\cdot 2(x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =24{\\int }_{-3}^{-4}\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =24{\\int }_{-3}^{-4}{u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =24\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-2})|}_{-3}^{-4} \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{12}{{u}^{2}})|}_{-3}^{-4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{(-4)^{2}}-(-\\frac{12}{(-3)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{16}-(-\\frac{12}{9}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-348282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c5691a04b5376867ac085f6aab3fcbfdc482e8ba035209a7afbe52b5ce1e830"} {"question" "q-348282" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "q-348282" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b0fb026152d6e4167de726b12396308550a1040b9fb444938029cb7027a75b8"} {"question" "e-458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\sqrt{x^2 + 1}\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/example-458.json" "file_sha256" "fcd6028fa579b211b7ee0143e2d77e90689257cde19f7dc8bbc5afda3a3abbe6"} {"question" "e-458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u = x^2+1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\cdot x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\overset{u-1}{\\overset{⏞}{{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\overset{\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u}{\\overset{⏞}{x\\,\\text{d}x}} \\\\  & =\\int (u-1)\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (u-1){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{3/2}-{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({x}^{2}+1)^{5/2}-\\frac{1}{3}({x}^{2}+1)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)^{5}}-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/example-458.json" "file_sha256" "fcd6028fa579b211b7ee0143e2d77e90689257cde19f7dc8bbc5afda3a3abbe6"} {"question" "e-457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{1/2}x(1-2x)^5\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/example-457.json" "file_sha256" "1fd9c280ec3923aa5b7f8fe92be0016e20a00c257836c6eb673a8a3dc50d288a"} {"question" "e-457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=1-2x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x = \\dfrac 1 2 (1-u).$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $1/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}x(1-2x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (1-u)\\cdot {u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{0}(1-u)\\cdot {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{0}({u}^{5}-{u}^{6})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{(\\frac{1}{6}{u}^{6}-\\frac{1}{7}{u}^{7})|}_{1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}([0-0]-[\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{7}]) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(-\\frac{1}{42}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{168}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042138/example-457.json" "file_sha256" "1fd9c280ec3923aa5b7f8fe92be0016e20a00c257836c6eb673a8a3dc50d288a"}] "usage" {"q-13191" [] "e-458" [] "e-457" []} "basis" 1533 "retractions" [[17592186064412 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $∫_{-2}^{0}x(x + 2)^{3}dx$."] [17592186063994 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\sqrt{x^2 + 1}\\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186063994 :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu = x^2+1\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{du}{dx} = 2x⟹\\frac{1}{2}du = xdx\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral in terms of $u$, and then express our final answer in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫x^{3}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}dx &= ∫x^{2} \\cdot x\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}dx \\\\\n&= ∫x^{2}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1} \\cdot xdx \\\\\n&= ∫x^{2}^(⏞)^(u - 1)\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1} \\cdot xdx^(⏞)^(\\frac{1}{2}du) \\\\\n&= ∫(u - 1)\\sqrt{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(u - 1)u^{1/2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(u^{3/2} - u^{1/2})du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{5}u^{5/2} - \\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}(x^{2} + 1)^{5/2} - \\frac{1}{3}(x^{2} + 1)^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(x^{2} + 1)^{5}} - \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{(x^{2} + 1)^{3}} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186063993 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{1/2}x(1-2x)^5\\,\\textrm d x$."] [17592186063993 :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1-2x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac 1 2 (1-u)\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x & 0 & 1/2 \\\\ u & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u$, remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1/2}x(1 - 2x)^{5}dx &= ∫_{1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (1 - u) \\cdot u^{5} \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}∫_{1}^{0}(1 - u) \\cdot u^{5}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}∫_{1}^{0}(u^{5} - u^{6})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{6}u^{6} - \\frac{1}{7}u^{7}) \\mid _{1}^{0} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}([0 - 0] - [\\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{1}{7}]) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(-\\frac{1}{42}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{168}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186061157 17592186061158 17592186061159 17592186061160 17592186061161] "immutable_fields" [[17592186061156 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061156 :answer-field/id] [17592186061156 :answer-field/key] [17592186061156 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
